export default {"X000104":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>An fpqc covering sieve with no fppf covering family</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000755\"><span>Fpqc covering sieve on the big site</span><code>P000755</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#X000104\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000104</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000754\"><span>Fppf covering sieve on the big site</span><code>P000754</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Sieves on the big category of schemes</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> For any field <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> use the sieve generated by <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec} k(t)\\to\\operatorname{Spec} k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. This affine faithfully flat morphism covers for fpqc. If a nonempty locally finitely presented <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-scheme factored through it, a nonempty affine neighbourhood of finite type would have a closed point with residue field finite over <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The factorization would embed <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> in that field over <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, a contradiction.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/022A\">Stacks 022A · fpqc coverings</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topologies/#tag-022A\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021N\">Stacks 021N · fppf coverings</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topologies/#tag-021N\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00FV\">Stacks 00FV · residue fields at maximal ideals of finite type algebras</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00FV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000104\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#X000104\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000103":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A totally separated space without a clopen basis</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000749\"><span>Totally separated space</span><code>P000749</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000053\"><span>Hausdorff space</span><code>P000053</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#X000103\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000103</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000064\"><span>Clopen basis (point-set zero dimensionality)</span><code>P000064</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000055\"><span>Profinite space</span><code>P000055</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Topological spaces</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Take the subspace <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝐑</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝐐</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝐍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\ell^2(\\mathbf R)\\cap\\mathbf Q^{\\mathbf N}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> with the norm topology. Distinct sequences differ in some coordinate. Cutting that coordinate at an irrational number strictly between the two values gives a clopen separation. Erdős proved that this separable metrizable space has dimension one, so it cannot have a clopen basis. Consequently it is not profinite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://www.renyi.hu/~p_erdos/1940-11.pdf\">P. Erdős, The dimension of the rational points in Hilbert space (1940), pp. 734–736</a> · <a href=\"https://topology.pi-base.org/spaces/S000142\">π-Base S000142 · Erdős space</a> · <a href=\"https://topology.pi-base.org/properties/P000048\">π-Base P000048 · Totally separated</a> · <a href=\"https://topology.pi-base.org/properties/P000050\">π-Base P000050 · Clopen basis</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08ZY\">Stacks 08ZY · profinite spaces and finite discrete quotients</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-08ZY\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000103\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#X000103\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000105":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>An injective map of spectra with two points after base change</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000772\"><span>Injective on underlying points</span><code>P000772</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000019\"><span>Finite</span><code>P000019</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000043\"><span>Surjective</span><code>P000043</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#X000105\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000105</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000044\"><span>Universally injective</span><code>P000044</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000773\"><span>Purely inseparable residue extensions everywhere</span><code>P000773</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Both <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> have one point. The residue extension is separable of degree two. Base change to <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> gives <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi><msub><mo>⊗</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C\\otimes_{\\mathbb R}\\mathbb C\\cong\\mathbb C\\times\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, with the two factors indexed by the identity and complex conjugation. Both source points map to the unique target point.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01S4\">Stacks 01S4 · criteria for universal injectivity</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01S4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CKN\">Stacks 0CKN · splitting a finite separable extension after scalar extension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/fields/#tag-0CKN\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/FT.pdf#page=107\">J. S. Milne, Fields and Galois Theory, v5.10, proof of Proposition 8.6(c) ⇒ (a), applied to the two roots of the minimal polynomial of i</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000105\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#X000105\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000106":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A finite surjective morphism flat on just one component</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000019\"><span>Finite</span><code>P000019</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000043\"><span>Surjective</span><code>P000043</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#X000106\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000106</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000006\"><span>Flat</span><code>P000006</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Fix a prime <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℤ</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℤ</mi><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔽</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Z\\to\\mathbb Z\\times\\mathbb F_p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> induces a finite surjective morphism. On the first component it is the identity. At the point of the second component the local ring map is <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℤ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔽</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Z_{(p)}\\to\\mathbb F_p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Multiplication by <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is injective on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℤ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Z_{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Tensoring with <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔽</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb F_p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> turns this injection into the zero endomorphism of a nonzero module. Thus flatness holds at every source point of the first component and fails at the point of the second.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01U3\">Stacks 01U3 · flatness at a point and at every point</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01U3\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00HD\">Stacks 00HD · flat modules preserve injections</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00HD\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-658-30733-2_15\">U. Görtz and T. Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry I, second edition, Definition 14.1(1),(3), testing the two local ring maps independently</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000106\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#X000106\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
